==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Rascals Card}}
*The Rascals can be used similarly to a [[Knight]] and [[Archers]] combo, albeit for 1 less Elixir and with more fragile but stronger “Archers” as well as a weaker but bulkier “Knight”. The Rascal Girls can be used to attack air troops similarly to the Archers, while the Rascal Boy can be used in the same way as a Knight.
*Left alone, this [[Cards|card]] can inflict massive damage towards, if not completely destroy, a [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]], regardless of the [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troop]] used. Always aim to destroy the Rascal Girls first, as they deal more damage per second than the Rascal Boy.
*Similar to Archers, the Rascals can be split if they are placed in the middle of the [[Arenas|Arena]]. A Rascal Girl will leave the group and go towards the other lane, helping to defend. The lone Rascal Girl will get 1 hit on the Crown Tower, and her respectable damage output means putting a cheap tank in front of her like an [[Ice Golem]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Knight]], or a [[Miner]] is not a bad idea to force a response out of the opponent.
**By splitting them at the center, the Rascals can counter the Royal Recruits for a +2 [[Elixir]] trade, with even a single Rascal Girl surviving for a possible counterpush.
*The Rascals are weak to a large variety of [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]], with some of them being able to OHKO the Rascal Girls while doing some chip damage to the Rascal Boy.
**[[The Log]], [[Arrows]], and [[Royal Delivery]] are excellent at countering this card, as they OHKO the Rascal Girls which is a part of damage. Knowing this, it is not a bad idea to use the Rascals with other spell-vulnerable cards, as the opponent may be forced to spread their spells thin. [[Goblin Barrel]] in particular synergizes well as the boy will survive with a majority of his health and can tank for the [[Goblins]] spawned from the Goblin Barrel.
**The [[Barbarian Barrel]] is also a very good counter to this card for a positive Elixir trade. The spell cripples the Rascal Girls, while the [[Barbarians|Barbarian]] finishes them off and defeats the Rascal Boy with a Crown Tower's assistance. However, in a larger [[Basics of Battle|battle]] with support [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]], the Barbarian may not be able to finish off the Rascal Girls.
**The high Elixir cost of the card makes it weak to a [[Poison]] spell. The Poison is able to 3HKO the Rascal Girls while also doing some notable damage to the Rascal Boy.
**[[Fireball]] can be used against the Rascals, similarly to the Poison. It will OHKO the Rascal Girls, and deal some damage to the Rascal Boy. Interestingly, the Rascal Boy is affected by knockback, allowing the Fireball to knock the Rascal Boy, possibly causing him to retarget.
**If the player wants to ensure that the Rascal Boy will not be a threat, [[Lightning]] and [[Rocket]] can be used against the trio. Although the Rascal Boy will survive, he will be too weak to pose a threat. However, they are both a negative Elixir trade, so try to hit something else as well with the latter.
*The [[Valkyrie]] is an effective counter to the Rascals, if placed properly, for a positive Elixir trade, since she can destroy the Rascal Girls in one spin and then finish off the Rascal Boy, and can counterpush with most of her hitpoints remaining.
*The [[Executioner]] and the [[Bowler]] are great counters to them, as they can splash all 3 Rascals and survive for a counterpush. However, on defense, the player can place the Rascals in such a way that the Bowler or Executioner target the Rascal Boy, allowing the Rascal Girls to survive and deal damage to them.
*The [[Mega Knight]] is also a great counter, since his spawn damage instantly kills the Rascal Girls and can quickly kill the Rascal Boy with almost no hitpoints lost, and can be used in a counter-push.
*They are great counters against tanks (along with the help of a Crown Tower) such as the [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], Mega Knight, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Boss Bandit]], and [[Mighty Miner]] for a positive Elixir trade, as the Rascal Boy will absorb all the damage while the Rascal Girls will continuously hit the tank.
*They can be an effective counter to the [[Graveyard]]; the Rascal Girls will attack 2 Skeletons at a time, along with the [[Tower Princess]] while the Rascal Boy tanks some hits from the Skeletons. This is a neutral Elixir trade and sets them for a counterpush. However, beware of spells that could destroy the Rascal Girls, like Arrows and Poison, as the Rascal Boy will not be able to keep up.
*When defending against a [[Golem]] or [[Balloon]], it's a good idea to put the Rascals away from the path of the Golem or Balloon, such that the Rascal Girls do not take death damage. This tactic should also be used against the [[Electro Giant]], to avoid the Rascal Girls being destroyed by the Electro Giant's Zap Pack.
*It is always a good idea to separate the Rascal Boy from the Rascal Girls to prevent the Rascal Girls from getting killed by area damage. This can be done by putting a large tank (for example the Electro Giant) amid the Rascals. On defense, the Rascals should be placed slightly earlier to allow the Rascal Boy to separate from the Rascal Girls so that any area damage support behind the troop that the Rascals are defending against would not gain value by hitting the Rascal Girls.
*The Rascals can counter 2 of the split [[Three Musketeers]] with the help of a [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troop]]. Both the tower troop and the Rascal Girls will deal damage to the [[Musketeer|Musketeers]] while the Rascal Boy tanks for them.
*The Rascals pair well with the [[X-Bow]] and [[Mortar]]. The Rascal Boy's high hitpoints acts as a meat-shield for the building, buying it more time to deal damage, while the Rascal Girls will target air troops that the buildings are unable to target.
*Similarly, they can also work with a Balloon. The Rascal Boy acts as a tank for the Balloon while the Rascal Girls handle air troops that are threatening the Balloon. Unlike Archers, the Rascal Girls are able to 2HKO [[Minions]] that are usually used against the Balloon.
*The Rascals have great synergy with the [[Skeleton Barrel]]. Both of them can act as bait for spells and their difference in ranges will force the opponent to use spells on one of the swarms, with the other swarm being protected by the Rascal Boy.
*They can work quite well with a [[Dark Prince]]. The Dark Prince adds splash damage to the trio, improving their matchup against swarms, while he also pushes the Rascal Boy closer to a target thanks to increased speed from his charge.

