==History==
2018
*The Rascals were once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Rascals Draft Challenge]], which started on 11/5/2018. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Rascals. If the player achieved 12 wins, they obtained the Rascals early.
*From 18/5/2018 through 22/5/2018, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 9+ players could buy an unlimited number of special Fortune [[Chests]] at the normal price that guarantee at least 50% of the Chest's contents to be Rascals. The Chest was able to generate up to 110% of its contents to be Rascals.
*The Rascals [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 25/5/2018.
*On 2/7/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/7/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Rascal Boy's hitpoints by 5.3% and increased the Rascal Girls' first attack time interval to 1 second (from 0.4 seconds).
2019
*On 4/3/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2019)|Balance Update]], gave the Rascals a new 0.15 seconds deploy stagger from each other.
*On 11/3/2019, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (11/3/2019)|maintenance break]] changed the deployment of the Rascals by making the Rascal Boy spawn first instead of the Rascal Girls.
*On 3/6/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/6/2019)|Balance Update]], increased the Rascal Boy’s attack time interval to 1.5 seconds (from 1.3 seconds), and his first attack time interval to 0.4 seconds (from 0.3 seconds).
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], decreased the Rascal Boy's range to 0.8 tiles (from 1 tile), now classified as Melee: Short.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Rascals' card info screen.
2020
*On 2/6/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/6/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the deploy stagger for each Rascal to 0.1 seconds (from 0.15 seconds).
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], decreased the Rascal Girls' first attack time interval to 0.8 seconds (from 1 second). It also moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Rascals from Jungle Arena to Rascal’s Hideout.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
*On 7/12/2021, the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(7/12/2021)|2021 Quarter 4 Update]], decreased the Rascal Girls’ attack time interval to 1 second (from 1.1 seconds).
2023
*On 4/4/2023, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(4/4/2023)|Balance Update]], increased the Rascal Boy's hitpoints by 6%, and decreased the Rascal Girls' first attack time interval to 0.5 second (from 0.8 seconds). It also increased the distance between the Rascals upon deployment.
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], made it so that Rascals' spawn formation would be correctly mirrored depending on which side of the Arena they were placed.
*On 8/7/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/7/2025)|Balance Update]], increased the Rascal Boy's damage by 54%, and decreased the Rascal Girls' damage by 6%.

